% Repeat structures from the ABC standard 2.1 (sections 4.8, 4.9 and 3.1.9),
% each padded out into a small tune for the abcnotes test suite. The notes
% are made up; the bar lines are the point.

X:1
T:First and second ending
N:the example in standard 2.1 section 4.9
M:6/8
L:1/8
K:D
faf gfe|[1 dfe dBA:|[2 d2e dcB|]

X:2
T:Double colon
N:a :: bar line ends one repeat and starts the next (section 4.8)
M:2/4
L:1/8
K:C
|: ABcd | efga :: bagf | edcB :|

X:3
T:Three times
N:|:: and ::| mark a section that is played three times (section 4.8)
M:2/4
L:1/8
K:C
|:: ABcd | efga ::|

X:4
T:Four passes
N:ending numbers may be lists: [1,3 [2 [4 (section 4.9)
M:2/4
L:1/8
P:A
K:C
P:A
|: ABcd |[1,3 efga :|[2 bagf :|[4 edcB |]

X:5
T:Parts
N:P:ABAB in the header gives the order of the P:A and P:B parts in the body (section 3.1.9)
M:2/4
L:1/8
P:ABAB
K:C
P:A
ABcd | efga ||
P:B
bagf | edcB |]
